Exercise
In this exercise, you’ll work once again with the prefab you made earlier in this hour. This time,
you will instantiate objects of the prefab by using code and hopefully have some fun with it:
1. Create a new scene in the same project where you’re storing the Lamp prefab. Click the
Lamp prefab in the Project view and change its position to (-1, 0, -5).
2. Delete the Directional Light game object from the scene.
3. Add an empty game object to the scene and rename it Spawn Point. Position it at (1, 1, -5).
Add a plane to your scene and position it at (0, 0, -4) with a rotation of (270, 0, 0).
4. Add a script to your project. Name the script PrefabGenerator and attach it to the spawn
point object. Listing 11.1 shows the complete code for the PrefabGenerator script.
